\f0\fs24 \cf0 # Section 4 Figures and Data\
\
This folder contains the **figures** and **data** used in Section 4 of the paper.  \
Specifically, it includes:\
\
- `fig16`, `fig19`, and `fig22` plot images  \
- Raw data used to generate these figures  \
- Python scripts to regenerate figures from data  \
\
---\
\
## 
\f1 \uc0\u55357 \u56615 
\f0  How to Generate Figures\
\
To generate the figures from data, run the following commands from within the `section4/` folder:\
\
```bash\
python recistapp_fig16.py 1\
```\
This will generate **Figure 16**.\
\
```bash\
python recistapp_fig18.py 1\
```\
This will generate **Figure 18**.\
\
```bash\
python revistApp_fig19bc.py 2\
```\
This will generate **Figure 19b**.\
\
```bash\
python revistApp_fig19bc.py 1\
```\
This will generate **Figure 19c**.\
\
```bash\
python revistApp_rfeats_fig22.py 1\
```\
This will generate **Figure 22**.\
\
---\
\
## 
\f1 \uc0\u55357 \u56550 
\f0  Notes\
\
- Please make sure the required dependencies (e.g., `matplotlib`, `numpy`, `pandas`) are installed.\
- Each script takes a numeric argument (e.g., `1` or `2`) to indicate the figure variant.\
- All outputs are saved in the same folder unless otherwise specified in the script.\
\
